11:32.203 --> 11:34.437
Thank you.

11:35.605 --> 11:37.339
Um, rupert?

11:37.341 --> 11:40.842
You know how we promised
never to lie to each other?

11:40.844 --> 11:42.545
Well, I lied earlier tonight.

11:42.547 --> 11:45.614
It's not a burn from
dunkin' donuts coffee.

11:45.616 --> 11:46.883
It's herpes.

11:46.885 --> 11:48.218
You should get yourself tested.

11:48.220 --> 11:49.586
Chris:
Hey, stewie.

11:49.588 --> 11:51.055
(gasps)
how long have you
been there?

11:51.057 --> 11:52.623
Long enough to know
you have herpes

11:52.625 --> 11:54.858
And do weird stuff
with your teddy bear.

11:54.860 --> 11:56.427
Yeah, he does weird stuff.

11:56.429 --> 11:58.096
I-I just don't stop him.

11:58.098 --> 12:01.233
Yeah, well, I just wanted to
let you know you're not alone.

12:01.235 --> 12:02.868
Oh, yeah? How so?

12:05.139 --> 12:07.272
Good lord!
You've got herpes, too?

12:07.274 --> 12:10.609
This house is like backstage
at a whitesnake concert!

12:10.611 --> 12:13.313
Not only that, but I
also got it from brian.

12:13.315 --> 12:15.081
We're blood brothers, too.

12:15.083 --> 12:16.717
You... You are?

12:16.719 --> 12:19.586
Yup, he knew he had herpes
and he didn't say anything.

12:19.588 --> 12:21.388
Maybe he was mad
I gave him fleas.

12:21.390 --> 12:22.722
I don't know.

12:22.724 --> 12:23.991
That bastard!

12:23.993 --> 12:25.760
Well, we need
to teach him a lesson.

12:25.762 --> 12:27.061
He's a menace.

12:27.063 --> 12:29.898
Like that coked-up giraffe
at studio 54.

12:30.834 --> 12:32.501
Yup, yup, people are watching.

12:32.503 --> 12:34.736
I'm that good.

12:38.976 --> 12:40.176
Are you donna summer?

12:40.178 --> 12:41.577
Why, yes, I am.

12:41.579 --> 12:43.347
I just want to thank you
for helping me reach

12:43.349 --> 12:46.583
A state of cocaine-fueled
1970s euphoria.

12:46.585 --> 12:48.151
Robert mapplethorpe?

12:48.153 --> 12:50.187
Can I put this fire extinguisher
someplace interesting

12:50.189 --> 12:51.856
And take your picture?

12:51.858 --> 12:54.159
I would love that!

13:02.134 --> 13:04.537
Um, uh, meg,
can you, um...

13:04.539 --> 13:05.871
Can you please
pass the milk?

13:05.873 --> 13:06.939
Shut up, dad.

13:06.941 --> 13:08.008
Okay, okay. I'm sorry.

13:08.010 --> 13:09.374
I'm sorry. I'll shut up.
What?!

13:09.376 --> 13:10.643
She-she's right, lois.
She's right.

13:10.645 --> 13:11.844
I-I don't need milk.

13:11.846 --> 13:13.612
I'll just moisten
my cereal with spit.

13:13.614 --> 13:14.681
(spits)

13:14.683 --> 13:15.982
Mmm, mmm, good spit.

13:15.984 --> 13:17.984
Peter, what the
hell is going on?

13:17.986 --> 13:20.221
Please tell me this isn't still
about how you punked out

13:20.223 --> 13:22.122
In front of those
guys at the clam.

13:22.124 --> 13:23.223
Oh, god, you're angry.

13:23.225 --> 13:24.292
I'll clean the dishes.

13:24.294 --> 13:25.859
Peter, stop it!

13:25.861 --> 13:27.662
Are... Are you crying?

13:27.664 --> 13:28.730
(crying):
No!

13:28.732 --> 13:30.198
Oh, this is insane.

13:30.200 --> 13:32.201
Peter, I want you
to March down to the clam

13:32.203 --> 13:35.002
Right now and get
your booth back.

13:35.004 --> 13:36.972
Oh my god, lois, you're right.

13:36.974 --> 13:39.841
If they see me crying, they'll
have to give us our booth back.

13:39.843 --> 13:43.146
No! I'm saying you got to go
down there and take it back.

13:43.148 --> 13:44.682
Like a man.

13:44.684 --> 13:47.050
Yeah.
I mean, I mean, yeah!

13:47.052 --> 13:49.587
I am going to the clam and
I'm getting my booth back.

13:49.589 --> 13:50.987
And, meg, you're gay.

13:50.989 --> 13:51.922
No, I'm not.

13:51.924 --> 13:52.990
You like guys, right?

13:52.992 --> 13:54.059
Yeah.

13:54.061 --> 13:55.659
Yeah, that's
called being gay.

14:03.402 --> 14:04.436
Hey.

14:04.438 --> 14:05.905
Uh, hey, kevin.

14:05.907 --> 14:08.841
You, uh... You smell
like a rabbit, buddy.

14:08.843 --> 14:10.844
Did something just
happen with a rabbit?

14:10.846 --> 14:13.379
I'll go get my dad.

14:13.381 --> 14:14.614
Listen, you guys.

14:14.616 --> 14:15.849
I think we're
all suffering

14:15.851 --> 14:17.116
From what happened
down at the clam.

14:17.118 --> 14:18.552
Yeah, I had to
start taking pills

14:18.554 --> 14:20.554
So I'd stop
thinking about it.

14:20.556 --> 14:22.123
Quagmire, that's a cialis.

14:22.125 --> 14:24.293
That's right, I'm not
thinking about it anymore.

14:24.295 --> 14:26.393
I'm thinking
about that couch.

14:26.395 --> 14:28.129
Well, I think
we gave up too easy.

14:28.131 --> 14:30.098
We need to March
back down to the clam

14:30.100 --> 14:31.467
And take back what's ours.

14:31.469 --> 14:33.301
He's right.
We need to sit up to those guys.

14:33.303 --> 14:34.570
No way.

14:34.572 --> 14:36.039
You want to get
yourselves killed,

14:36.041 --> 14:37.138
That's your business,
but I'm not going.

14:37.140 --> 14:39.041
Fine, me and joe
will go without you.

14:39.043 --> 14:40.644
But just know
you're letting us down.

14:40.646 --> 14:42.211
We're supposed
to stick together.

14:42.213 --> 14:44.881
Like goatee guys
at a barbecue.

14:46.450 --> 14:48.753
Do you mind if I stand next
to you while we eat standing?

14:48.755 --> 14:50.086
No problem.

14:50.088 --> 14:51.554
Hey, let's go grab
some good beer

14:51.556 --> 14:53.823
Even though we
brought the bad beer.

14:53.825 --> 14:56.060
<i>Narrator:
And these two barbecue scumbags</i>

14:56.062 --> 14:57.962
<i>Formed a lifelong friendship</i>

14:57.964 --> 15:01.834
<i>Until their deaths
at the ripe old age of 52</i>

15:01.836 --> 15:05.837
<i>In separate atv accidents.</i>

15:09.243 --> 15:10.843
You know, I'm so glad
you finally agreed

15:10.845 --> 15:12.178
To go out with me, jenna.

15:12.180 --> 15:14.181
Me, too. I'm having
a really nice time.

15:14.183 --> 15:15.948
You seem like a great guy.

15:15.950 --> 15:17.918
Stewie:
Yes, thank you, we'll take
the table in the corner,

15:17.920 --> 15:19.118
Next to the herpes dog.

15:19.120 --> 15:20.688
Oh, hey, brian.

15:20.690 --> 15:22.122
And who's your date?

15:22.124 --> 15:24.325
Wow, you must be
such a good person

15:24.327 --> 15:27.528
To knowingly go out with
a herpes-riddled dirtbag.

15:27.530 --> 15:29.864
Ew! I'm sorry, brian.

15:29.866 --> 15:32.267
I-I've got to go.

15:32.269 --> 15:33.435
Damn it, you guys!

15:33.437 --> 15:35.604
Her dad's really rich!

15:38.843 --> 15:40.175
Wow, you weren't kidding.

15:40.177 --> 15:41.677
Yeah.

15:44.815 --> 15:47.050
Peter:
Hey, you bums!

15:47.052 --> 15:49.019
If you bastards
want our booth,

15:49.021 --> 15:51.122
You got to go
through us to get it.

15:51.124 --> 15:53.557
Smells like this guy's
already wet himself.

15:53.559 --> 15:54.992
Don't flatter yourself.

15:54.994 --> 15:56.394
That was from this morning.

15:56.396 --> 15:58.396
Oh, man, this is gonna be fun.

15:58.398 --> 16:00.666
Yeah, and there's only
two of you losers.

16:00.668 --> 16:01.967
Where's your skinny friend?

16:01.969 --> 16:03.802
(door opens)
quagmire:
Right here.

16:06.171 --> 16:07.873
Quagmire! You came!

16:07.875 --> 16:09.242
Sure did, peter.

16:09.244 --> 16:10.409
Thanks for calling me
skinny, by the way.

16:10.411 --> 16:11.845
I realized you
were right.

16:11.847 --> 16:13.346
If we don't stand up
for ourselves now,

16:13.348 --> 16:15.415
We'll regret it
for the rest of our lives.

16:15.417 --> 16:18.485
And this might be the stupidest
thing I've ever done, but...

16:18.487 --> 16:19.486
(grunts)

16:19.488 --> 16:22.288
Oh, now you're gonna get it.

16:24.893 --> 16:27.094
(grunts)

16:32.568 --> 16:34.302
Whelp, I'm out.

16:35.838 --> 16:37.173
Aah!

16:41.746 --> 16:43.345
Hey! That was my pool cue.

16:43.347 --> 16:44.947
I brought it from home.

16:44.949 --> 16:46.450
Oh, sorry.

16:46.452 --> 16:47.917
It screws together.

16:47.919 --> 16:50.087
And I even have
this special little case for it.

16:50.089 --> 16:51.922
I-I feel bad now. I...

16:51.924 --> 16:55.626
Aah!

16:55.628 --> 16:56.960
Hyah!

16:56.962 --> 16:58.730
Hey, that was my
pawtucket patriot sign.

16:58.732 --> 17:00.465
I brought it from home.

17:00.467 --> 17:02.935
Okay, now I'm starting
to doubt everything you said.

17:04.403 --> 17:05.771
(grunts)

17:05.773 --> 17:07.441
All right, guys,
I know this looks desperate,

17:07.443 --> 17:09.975
But I've got
this can of spinach.

17:22.990 --> 17:25.225
Aah!

17:46.516 --> 17:48.017
Aw, god, it's all watery.

17:48.019 --> 17:49.653
Aah!

17:49.655 --> 17:51.856
You know, I almost said
"no chairs" at the beginning.

17:53.860 --> 17:55.526
Haven't you guys
had enough?

17:55.528 --> 17:58.297
Why don't you just admit
you're beat and get out of here?

17:58.299 --> 17:59.530
Both:
Okay.

17:59.532 --> 18:00.966
No! Never!

18:00.968 --> 18:02.867
We will never stop fighting
for this booth.

18:02.869 --> 18:04.803
This booth is my home.

18:04.805 --> 18:06.272
I was born in this booth.

18:06.274 --> 18:07.707
I was married in this booth.

18:07.709 --> 18:09.943
My children were all conceived
in this booth.

18:09.945 --> 18:12.712
Hell, I witnessed every
significant historical event

18:12.714 --> 18:14.347
In my lifetime right here!

18:14.349 --> 18:16.782
<i>I was in this booth
when the challenger exploded.</i>

18:16.784 --> 18:19.052
Oh, my god, no!

18:19.054 --> 18:21.121
I was in this booth on 9/11.

18:21.123 --> 18:23.224
Oh, my god, no!

18:23.226 --> 18:26.126
I was in this booth when
president obama was elected.

18:26.128 --> 18:28.195
Oh, my god, no!

18:28.197 --> 18:30.498
So, if you want this booth,
you're gonna have

18:30.500 --> 18:33.369
To pry it
from my cold, dead hands.

18:33.371 --> 18:35.170
Why are we even bothering
with these idiots?

18:35.172 --> 18:37.907
We're shipping out to
afghanistan tomorrow.

18:37.909 --> 18:39.408
You guys are soldiers?

18:39.410 --> 18:41.644
It's our
third tour of duty.

18:43.581 --> 18:45.815
(applause)

18:49.152 --> 18:51.822
If I could touch my own head,
I'd salute you.

18:51.824 --> 18:53.924
(grunting)

18:53.926 --> 18:56.260
With his head,
I salute you.

18:56.262 --> 18:58.496
Everyone,
I declare this to be

18:58.498 --> 19:00.432
These three guys day.

19:00.434 --> 19:03.367
And not
these three guys day.

19:03.369 --> 19:05.670
(cheering)

19:11.679 --> 19:15.481
I can't believe I have
to root for afghanistan now.

19:18.953 --> 19:19.954
(computer chimes)

19:19.956 --> 19:21.355
Ah, damn it!

19:23.959 --> 19:25.560
Stewie! Chris!

19:25.562 --> 19:26.760
Yes, brian?

19:26.762 --> 19:28.562
You hacked my
facebook account!

19:28.564 --> 19:30.731
Oh, yes, we actually just
changed your profile picture.

19:30.733 --> 19:32.167
(computer dings)

19:34.404 --> 19:36.572
Aah! Damn it!
Look, enough, okay?

19:36.574 --> 19:38.475
What the hell do you
guys want from me?!

19:38.477 --> 19:39.741
I want to drive
your prius

19:39.743 --> 19:41.944
To the end of the block
all by myself.

19:41.946 --> 19:43.412
That's it?
Yes.

19:43.414 --> 19:44.981
Okay.

19:44.983 --> 19:46.883
Yay!

19:48.052 --> 19:50.221
(engine starts)

19:54.893 --> 19:57.662
That's, uh... That's way past
the end of the block.

19:57.664 --> 19:58.896
Yeah, his room's empty.

19:58.898 --> 20:00.231
I don't think
he's coming back.

20:00.233 --> 20:01.432
Huh.

20:01.434 --> 20:02.768
Well, what about you?

20:02.770 --> 20:04.636
I want to go on a date
with neve campbell

20:04.638 --> 20:07.106
So I can give her a
nice ladle of stew.

20:07.108 --> 20:09.675
What? How am I supposed
to even find her?

20:09.677 --> 20:11.845
Damn it, stewie, why are you
being so vindictive?

20:11.847 --> 20:14.280
Because, brian,
for the first time in my life,

20:14.282 --> 20:16.317
I realized I couldn't trust you.

20:16.319 --> 20:19.552
I couldn't trust
my own best friend.

20:20.489 --> 20:23.157
(sighs)
I... I'm sorry, stewie.

20:23.159 --> 20:25.826
You're right. I let you down.

20:25.828 --> 20:28.263
I guess... I guess
I was just too embarrassed

20:28.265 --> 20:29.697
To admit I had herpes.

20:29.699 --> 20:31.599
It was a rotten thing to do,

20:31.601 --> 20:34.269
And I promise I will
never lie to you again.

20:34.271 --> 20:35.871
Thanks, brian.

20:35.873 --> 20:37.873
That's all I really wanted.

20:37.875 --> 20:40.309
So, do you forgive me?

20:40.311 --> 20:42.611
Yes. I do.

20:44.648 --> 20:47.216
So, I'm gonna have herpes
for the rest of my life, huh?

20:47.218 --> 20:49.720
Yeah, but most of the time,
it won't even be an issue.

20:49.722 --> 20:51.855
It only really flares up
during periods of great stress.

20:51.857 --> 20:54.657
Like your wedding day
or a big job interview.

20:54.659 --> 20:58.296
So, what would you say some
of your weaknesses are?

20:58.298 --> 21:00.899
That... That-that's
probably one of them.

21:00.900 --> 22:01.906
Thank you for watching «Family Guy» on
www.FOX-fan.ru